{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963586,"nonce":"hIfPknn3uGZ+jvPqG05t25q9gRw=","title":"An abstract's own toString is ignored by string concatenation","message":"Row: Issue4966.\n\nString interpolation desugars to `Binary Add` (tast_to_hir.rs StringInterpolation arm). MIR concat\n(ir/mir/expr/operators.rs) asks `try_call_tostring`, which handles classes only, and\n`convert_to_string_with_hint` (ir/mir/types.rs) has no Abstract arm, so `int_to_string` runs on\nthe abstract's representation. `user_tostring_symbol`, which handles abstracts, is used only by\nthe Std.string intrinsic. Also `\"n: \" + Named(\"x\")` over String prints `n: x` (Haxe: the\nabstract's toString).","files":null}]}